{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_page", "label": "CPU-bound work", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_cpu_bound_work", "label": "CPU-bound work", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Busy work (JSON.parse of 50MB, image resize, bcrypt sync, ReDoS) holds the single thread. Waiting I/O is fine. Node's genuine weakness; the fix is never async."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_async_does_not_yield", "label": "async does not stop blocking", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "async changes the return value, not whether the body blocks. There is no await that makes a for loop yield."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_chunking_setimmediate", "label": "Chunk CPU work with setImmediate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Yield to check so pending I/O runs. Aim 10\u201350ms per chunk. Improves others' latency, not throughput. Occasional work that splits naturally."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_worker_threads", "label": "worker_threads for CPU work", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Real parallelism on another thread. Spawning is expensive \u2014 use a piscina pool, not one worker per request. Data copies via structured clone; transfer ArrayBuffers."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_libuv_async_crypto", "label": "Async crypto on the libuv thread pool", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "crypto.pbkdf2, scrypt and async bcrypt run off the loop; *Sync variants block it. Often the cheapest real fix."}, {"id": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_delay_metric_blind_spot", "label": "Event loop delay misses a fully blocked loop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sampled by a timer that cannot fire while blocked. A 1.2s block reported worst gap 0ms because it recorded no samples. Missing data is the signal."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_page", "target": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_cpu_bound_work", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_async_does_not_yield", "target": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_cpu_bound_work", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/nodejs/pages/phase-2-async/22-cpu-bound-work.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bound_work_page", "target": "docs_nodejs_pages_phase_2_async_22_cpu_bou